Title: Mitti Ke Sher
Credit: Sample script written for the offline reader (realistic style, no ages or CAPS help in places)
Author: Screenplay Breakdown test suite

EXT. SONPUR VILLAGE - AKHADA - DAWN #1#

Mist over a mud wrestling pit. BALDEV, a heavy-set former wrestler in a faded langot, rakes the mud with a wooden spade. A rooster crows somewhere.

His daughters SAVITRI and KAMLA, both in oversized shorts and their brother's old t-shirts, jog around the pit. Savitri carries a brick in each hand.

BALDEV
Ten more rounds. Then the rope.

KAMLA
Bauji, my legs are finished.

Baldev tosses her a steel tumbler of milk. Kamla catches it, spills half.

A few village boys sit on the boundary wall, laughing. One of them, Pappu, whistles.

Savitri drops the bricks, picks up a clod of mud and flings it at Pappu.

INT. BALDEV'S HOUSE - COURTYARD - DAY #2#

SHANTI, Baldev's wife, kneads dough on a brass plate. A buffalo is tied to a neem tree. Two hens peck near the hand pump.

Savitri and Kamla enter, caked in mud. Shanti looks at their filthy clothes and shakes her head.

SHANTI
Who will marry these two?

Dadi sits on a charpai in the corner, shelling peas into a bowl. She says nothing.

Baldev enters with a pair of hair clippers and a white towel.

SAVITRI / KAMLA
No!

Shanti grabs the clippers. Baldev takes them back.

BALDEV (CONT'D)
Long hair is a handle for the opponent.

He drapes the towel over Savitri's shoulders. Her braid falls on the floor. Kamla's eyes fill with tears.

EXT. VILLAGE SCHOOL - DAY #3#

Savitri and Kamla, heads cropped, walk through the gate in their school uniforms, bags on their shoulders. Students stare. A teacher rings the bell.

Pappu and two other boys block the way.

PAPPU
Arre, pehelwan sisters!

Kamla swings her school bag at him. Pappu falls into a puddle. The students cheer.

Masterji hurries over, cane in hand.

EXT. HIGHWAY DHABA - NIGHT #4#

A truck stop. Three trucks are parked in a row. Drivers eat at wooden tables under a tube light.

Baldev arrives on his old scooter with Savitri riding pillion. He takes a folded poster out of his kurta pocket: "DISTRICT DANGAL - PRIZE 500 RUPEES".

BALDEV
(to the dhaba owner)
Two chai. And a plate of chicken for her.

The DHABA OWNER, a bald man in a stained vest, stares at Savitri.

DHABA OWNER
Chicken? For a girl?

A stray dog sniffs at Savitri's sandals. She feeds it a piece of roti.

EXT. DISTRICT DANGAL GROUND - DAY #5#

Hundreds of spectators crowd around a mud pit. Dhol players beat their drums. A banner flutters over the stage. The REFEREE, in a white shirt and a whistle around his neck, raises his hand.

Savitri, in a borrowed singlet, faces a boy twice her size. Baldev watches from the edge, a gamcha around his neck.

REFEREE
Kushti shuru!

The boy charges. Savitri ducks, grabs his leg and throws him. Dust rises. The crowd roars.

The boy slams her on her back. She twists free, blood on her lip.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
What a fight! The girl is not giving up!

The referee blows the whistle. The boy's hand is raised. A man in the crowd throws a fifty-rupee note at Savitri's feet.

Baldev picks up the note and presses it into her palm.

INT. BALDEV'S HOUSE - BEDROOM - NIGHT #6#

A lantern burns low. Savitri lies on a cot, a wet cloth on her bruised eye. Shanti rubs turmeric paste on her elbow.

On the wall hangs a framed photograph of Baldev's father in a wrestler's turban, a silver mace in his hands.

SHANTI
(softly)
Your grandfather won that mace in Lahore.

Kamla is asleep beside them, hugging a pillow. A transistor radio plays an old film song.

BALDEV (O.S.)
She sleeps now. Tomorrow, four o'clock.

EXT. SONPUR VILLAGE - AKHADA - DAY #7#

SUPER: EIGHT YEARS LATER

The mud pit is now a blue wrestling mat under a tin shed. Savitri, in a red tracksuit, lifts a barbell. Kamla skips with a rope.

A white Ambassador car pulls up. COACH MEHRA, in sunglasses and a navy blazer, steps out with a clipboard. His driver waits by the car.

COACH MEHRA
Baldev-ji? I am from the National Sports Academy.

Baldev wipes his hands on his gamcha. He does not offer a chair.

Mehra opens a file and takes out two forms and a pen.

INT. NATIONAL SPORTS ACADEMY - HOSTEL ROOM - NIGHT #8#

Two iron beds. Savitri unpacks a tin trunk: singlets, a pair of wrestling shoes, a jar of ghee, her grandfather's photograph.

Her roommate RITU lies on the other bed, painting her nails, a mobile phone pressed to her ear.

RITU
(into phone)
No, yaar, the new one is from some village.

Savitri places a small idol of Hanuman on the windowsill and lights an incense stick.

RITU (CONT'D)
(covering the phone)
You can't light that here. Fire alarm.

INT. BALDEV'S HOUSE - COURTYARD - DAY #9#

Baldev, older now, sits on the charpai, watching a small television. On the screen, Savitri walks out in an India jersey.

Dadi, Shanti and a dozen neighbours crowd around. Children sit on the floor. A goat wanders in; Shanti shoos it away with a broom.

COMMENTATOR (V.O.)
And from Sonpur village, Savitri Kumari!

The electricity goes. The screen dies. Groans.

Baldev picks up his walking stick, goes to the tractor and starts hooking up its battery with a pair of cables.

INT. STADIUM - WRESTLING ARENA - NIGHT #10#

Floodlights. Thousands of fans wave flags. Savitri and her opponent, a RUSSIAN WRESTLER, circle each other on the mat. A doctor and two paramedics wait with a stretcher near the tunnel.

The Russian wrestler lifts Savitri and drops her. The scoreboard reads 4-1.

Savitri looks up at the stands. Kamla, Ritu and Coach Mehra are on their feet. Her father's seat is empty.

She wipes the sweat from her eyes, tightens her knee bandage and stands up.

The whistle. Savitri shoots for the legs, lifts, and slams her opponent flat. The crowd erupts. Confetti falls.

A medal is hung around her neck. The national flag rises.

EXT. STADIUM - CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS #11#

A locked storeroom door. Banging from inside. A security guard fumbles with a bunch of keys.

The door opens. Baldev stumbles out, sweating, his kurta torn at the shoulder. From the arena, the national anthem.

He stands still and listens. He knows.
